Strong pre-orders have reportedly prompted Apple to order millions more <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> units from suppliers, according to <a href="https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261022PD219/iphone-apple-shipments-demand-foldable.html"><em>DigiTimes</em></a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iPhone-Duo-Hinge-Feature-1.jpg" alt="" width="1886" height="1064" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1071750" /><br/>
Supply chain sources said Foxconn and component manufacturers had received instructions reflecting a roughly 44% increase from 9.7 million to 14 million devices. The revised target reportedly follows strong pre-orders for Apple's first foldable iPhone and covers a full 12-month period, rather than the remainder of 2026.<br/>
<br/>
Apple last week described demand as "<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/16/apple-iphone-duo-demand-extraordinary/">nothing short of extraordinary</a>." Within 30 minutes of pre-orders opening on October 16, U.S. shipping estimates had <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/16/iphone-duo-preorder-shipping-wait-times/">reached January 25</a> across all configurations. <br/>
<br/>
Meeting the higher shipment target could still prove challenging. <em><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/digitimes-com/">DigiTimes</a></em> said output would depend on assembly progress, following earlier reports of <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/29/iphone-duo-reportedly-facing-production-problems/">manufacturing difficulties</a> affecting assembly, displays, and hinges.<br/>
<br/>
<em>&zwnj;DigiTimes&zwnj;</em> forecasts that global foldable smartphone shipments will grow 25.7% in 2026 and 59.1% in 2027, compared with 7.4% growth in 2025, with Apple's entry expected to contribute to the expansion.<br/>
